# Local configuration and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Go build and test outputs
/bin/
/dist/
coverage.out
*.test
*.prof
/*.exe
/*.exe~

# Go caches pointed at the repository root. They must never be committed, and
# they are worth naming here for a second reason: several architecture gates walk
# the whole tree and parse every .go file they find, so a toolchain download
# landing under the root breaks the entire gate with a parse error coming out of
# Go's own testdata. Keep local caches outside the repository.
/.tmp-gocache/
/.tmp-gomodcache/

# Local multi-repository workspace only
go.work
go.work.sum

# Editors and local agent staging
.idea/
.vscode/
.codex-*
/.codex/
/output/

# Client apps under apps/ (Node toolchain)
node_modules/
apps/*/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Restricted evidence instances. AGENTS.md keeps only de-identified identifiers
# and evidence indices in the repository; the artefacts themselves live in the
# evidence store (ADR-0008). Rate cards belong to a tenant's supplier
# relationship, not to this product.
/docs/reference/**/*.xlsx
/docs/reference/**/*.xls
/docs/reference/**/*.pdf
/docs/*.rar
# Raw tenant webhook captures carry live credentials and recipient PII; only a
# de-identified evidence index may be committed in their place.
/docs/wooolink/

# Local agent scratch at the repo root
/parallel_prompt.md
# Numbered markdown at the repository root is always a session artefact that
# missed its home. Session output belongs under .scratch/<feature>/, and every
# tracked root file is named for what it is (AGENTS.md, README.md, compose.yaml).
# Chat exports and loose analyses landing here as 01.md/02.md dirty `git status`
# for every shared worktree at once, and the session that finds them cannot tell
# whose they are or whether they may be deleted.
/[0-9][0-9].md
# Helper scripts parked directly in .scratch/ are one-off local tooling. Scripts
# that belong to a feature live in that feature's directory and stay tracked.
/.scratch/*.ps1

# Produced by the IDP sidebar rather than maintained by hand (see
# .cursor/rules/idp-mcp-messenger.mdc), and it carries this host's loopback
# ports and absolute interpreter paths. Every host therefore rewrites it and
# every session sees it dirty, so it is deliberately not under version control.
# A fresh clone has no MCP channels until the sidebar writes this file.
/.cursor/mcp.json
